 can be generated from endogenous progenitors in injured adult mouse pancreas.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>132</volume><fpage>197</fpage><lpage>207</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18243096</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004827-Wang1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenberg</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>FW</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Tubular complexes as a source for islet neogenesis in the pancreas of diabetes-prone BB rats.</article-title><source>Laboratory Investigation</source><volume>85</volume><fpage>675</fpage><lpage>688</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15765120</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004827-Paris1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Paris</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Tourrel-Cuzin</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Plachot</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ktorza</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Review: Pancreatic beta-cell neogenesis revisited.</article-title><source>Experimental Diabetes Research</source><volume>5</volume><fpage>111</fpage><lpage>121</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004827-Meier1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Meier</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Butler</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Galasso</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Martinez</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Di